nestjs-zod (vendored copy)
==========================

Source: https://github.com/BenLorantfy/nestjs-zod (package `nestjs-zod`, version 5.5.0)
Upstream license: MIT (reproduced below).

What this vendored copy changes and why
---------------------------------------
Only `peerDependencies` and `peerDependenciesMeta` were REMOVED from package.json.
Upstream declares `@nestjs/common ^10 || ^11` and `@nestjs/swagger ^7 || ^8 || ^11`,
which do not cover the NestJS 12 / Swagger 12 stack of this template — that mismatch
is what forced `legacy-peer-deps=true` in `.npmrc`, hiding ALL peer conflicts on
every install. The runtime code (`dist/`) is byte-identical to upstream; every
declared peer is satisfied by this project's own dependencies, so the install
disagreement had no runtime meaning. With the peers gone, npm resolves the tree
strictly again and `.npmrc` needs no override.

Do not edit `dist/`. When upstream publishes a release whose peers include
Nest/Swagger 12, delete this folder and depend on the registry version again
(the AGENTS.md "Stack" section records the same exit criteria).

